>
  <h2>What a page on this site is allowed to claim</h2>
  <p>A price belongs on a page when it appears on the vendor’s pricing page, homepage, or official docs, with the date it was current. A product behavior belongs when the vendor’s docs or terms describe it. A recommendation belongs when it follows from that public record and from the job the reader described. A benchmark, a star rating, or a “measured X percent” line belongs only when this site ran that test and can show the method. This version of the site does not include original lab tests.</p>
  <h2>Where the 24 November 2026 figures come from</h2>
  <p>PostHog, Mixpanel, Amplitude, Fathom, and Google Analytics figures come from their public pricing or product pages. Plausible’s monthly ladder comes from the pricing slider data on plausible.io. DataFast does not publish a working /pricing URL (it returns 404). The monthly and yearly amounts come from the pricing data the homepage itself loads, and the plan limits come from the homepage FAQ and the terms. Bot-traffic overage pricing comes from the homepage and DataFast’s changelog. Cookieless behavior comes from DataFast’s tracking doc.</p>
  <p>A number that is not public is absent here. That includes Fathom’s dollar steps above 100,000 pageviews, PostHog’s identified-event rate card, PostHog platform-package fees, Amplitude’s Plus calculator steps, Mixpanel add-on fees, and any list price for Google Analytics 360.</p>
  <h2>How a recommendation is scoped</h2>
  <p>DataFast is recommended for revenue attribution. The product is built to join traffic to payments. It is not a full replacement for PostHog, Mixpanel, or Amplitude, which are product-analytics suites with replay, experiments, or feature flags. If acquisition is mostly Google Ads, or GA4 already feeds a warehouse the team uses, the guides say to stay. Affiliate links do not move a tool into a job it does not do.</p>
  <h2>What is outside this method</h2>
  <p>This site has not subscribed to every paid plan, interviewed customers, or run the same site through every tool for a month. A sentence that would require that work is left out. Readers who want a live feel of a product should use the vendor’s trial: DataFast is 14 days without a card, Plausible is 30 days without a card, and Fathom is 7 days with a card.</p>
  <p>The <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a> and <a href="/about/">about</a> page sit next to this one. Corrections can be sent from the <a href="/contact/">contact</a> page.</p>
</Simple>
